### Section 3: ViT Attention Hook Engine

The core grounding mechanism. Implements a reusable `VitAttentionCapture` class:

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  BLIP-2 EVA-ViT Encoder (Frozen)                │
│                                                   │
│  Image (224×224) → 16×16 patch grid (256 tokens) │
│                                                   │
│  Register forward hook on final encoder layer:    │
│    → Capture Q × K^T attention weights            │
│    → Average across heads → (256,) spatial map    │
│    → Reshape to (16, 16) → bilinear upsample      │
│    → Apply colourmap ('turbo') → alpha-blend       │
│    → Overlay on original satellite image            │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

**Key implementation details:**
- Hook target: `model.vision_model.encoder.layers[-1].self_attn` — captures the attention weights from the **final ViT encoder layer** where spatial features are most semantically meaningful
- Attention aggregation: Mean across all attention heads, then take the CLS token's attention to all 256 spatial patches → reshape to 16×16
- Upsampling: `F.interpolate(mode='bilinear')` to 224×224
- Normalisation: Min-max normalise to [0, 1]
- Visualisation: `matplotlib.cm.turbo` colourmap → RGBA → alpha-blend at 0.5 opacity over the original satellite image

