### Section 5: Evidence Generator — Model 2 (Cross-Modal Fusion)

**`fusion_evidence(optical_path, sar_path, question)`** → returns:

| Output | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| `answer` | Generated text from Model 2 |
| `optical_heatmap` | Attention overlay on the optical image |
| `sar_heatmap` | Attention overlay on the SAR image |
| `modality_contribution` | `{"optical": 0.63, "sar": 0.37}` — ratio of L2 norms of the 32 optical vs 32 SAR Q-Former query tokens |
| `dominant_sensor` | `"optical"` or `"sar"` — whichever contributed more |
| `description` | *"The model relied primarily on optical data (63%) for spectral features, supplemented by SAR (37%) for structural/texture confirmation. Attention concentrated on the central-south region of both images."* |

**Process:**
1. Load Model 2 from Drive
2. Register ViT attention hooks on **both** passes through the shared ViT (one for optical, one for SAR)
3. Run inference → capture both attention maps + Q-Former query outputs
4. Compute modality contribution: `‖opt_query‖₂ / (‖opt_query‖₂ + ‖sar_query‖₂)`
5. Generate dual overlay side-by-side plot + pie chart of modality contribution
6. Save to Drive

